// Diagnostic codes as values.
//
// `KiraError` names every code the compiler emits; this is how a code that
// arrived as text becomes one. A test that asserts `.KSEM061` therefore
// compares a value, and goes on comparing it after the message is reworded —
// which is the whole reason a code exists.
//
// One `if` per code rather than a `match`: `match` selects on an enum, and the
// question here is the other way round. Splitting the chain by code prefix was
// measured and made no difference — the analyzer is linear in declarations, so
// this costs what its 272 entries cost and no more.

// The code `text` names, or `.Unrecognized` when this enum does not list it.
function kiraErrorFromCode(text: borrow String) -> KiraError {
    if text == "KBE001" { return .KBE001 }
    if text == "KBE002" { return .KBE002 }
    if text == "KBE012" { return .KBE012 }
    if text == "KCL001" { return .KCL001 }
    if text == "KCL002" { return .KCL002 }
    if text == "KCL003" { return .KCL003 }
    if text == "KCL005" { return .KCL005 }
